      "problem": "Which of the following is a type I region in two-dimensional space?",
      "worked_solution": "A type I region can be written as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le x\\le b,\\,g(x)\\le y\\le f(x)\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nA type I region has the property that a vertical line drawn through the region intersects the region in a single interval only.\n\nAmong the given options, the only type I region is the following.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14252915/assets/fc79eeb10b320beb24a54e3cbbbaf8b539fc0c51cb9f6f8ac8127b6faeca1180.png)",
